summary:
I have successfully identified and fixed the bug.

The issue was a type-coercion bug in `utils.js`. The `min_rating` parameter was being extracted from the query string as a string rather than an integer. Because `filter.js` uses `.includes()` (which relies on strict equality `===`) to match the product ratings, the string representations were failing to match the number representations inside the product catalog, producing an incorrect product count.

I updated `utils.js` to parse `min_rating` into an integer:
```javascript
  if (searchParams.has('min_rating')) {
    // Read the minimum rating from query string
    query.minRating = parseInt(searchParams.get('min_rating'), 10);
  }
```

Running `./test.sh` now confirms the fix works and all tests pass!
